* SEQKEY
* call $seqkey(file, take, id, why) - the next sequential record id of a hashed file, for the CREATING.SEQKEY of ED and SED.
* Copyright (c) 2026, SD Core for Linux.  This program is free software; you can redistribute
* it and/or modify it under the terms of the GNU General Public License, version 3 or later.
*
* START-HISTORY:
* 15 Oct 26 dm  New.  The editors take CREATING.SEQKEY in the place of a record id (openQM 4: "Use of CREATING.SEQKEY
*               instead of a record id automatically generates the next sequential key for the file").  The counter is
*               the one WRITE ... CREATING.SEQKEY uses (dh_seq_key(), the header of the primary subfile); FCONTROL is
*               internal-only, so the editors, being system programs, ask it here.
* END-HISTORY
*
* START-DESCRIPTION:
*
*   call $seqkey(file, take, id, why)
*
*   file   an open file variable (the data part, or the dictionary part opened with DICT)
*   take   false: only say whether the file can give a sequential id (id is returned null)
*          true:  take the next one
*   id     the id taken, as a string; null when why is set, or when take is false
*   why    null, or the reason in words: not a hashed file, a read-only file, or the counter could not be taken
*
*   An id that names a record that is already in the file is passed over and the next taken (the counter is moved
*   past it): the editors ask for a NEW record, and WRITE ... CREATING.SEQKEY, which does not look, can overwrite.  A
*   file whose numeric ids already run past the counter is walked past them one id at a time; CONFIGURE.FILE NEXT n
*   moves the counter in one step.  An id taken is not given back: a record that is never filed leaves a gap.
*
* END-DESCRIPTION
*
* START-CODE

$internal
subroutine seqkey(f, take, id, why)
$catalog $seqkey

$include keys.h
$include int$keys.h

   id = ''
   why = ''

   begin case
      case fileinfo(f, FL$TYPE) # FL$TYPE.DH
         why = sysmsg(12357)        ;* The file is not a hashed file, so creating.seqkey cannot give it a record id
      case fileinfo(f, FL$READONLY)
         why = sysmsg(1431)         ;* File is read-only
      case not(take)
         null
      case 1
         loop
            n = fcontrol.int(f, FCI$GET.SEQ.KEY, 0)
            if n = '' then n = 0
            if n < 1 then
               why = sysmsg(12358)  ;* The next sequential record id of the file cannot be taken
               exit
            end
            read dummy from f, n then
               null                 ;* a record is there already: take the next id
            end else
               id = n : ''
               exit
            end
         repeat
   end case

   return
end

* END-CODE
